are going to support
Windows WinRM so that you

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:24.620
can kind of log in, run a bunch
of your PowerShell commands

00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:27.920
remotely to manage, like, your
fleet of Windows machines.

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:30.725
A really cool thing is also,
like, hey people start up VMs

00:10:30.725 --> 00:10:33.000
and you definitely want
to RDP into it and say,

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:35.520
hey, I can connect to my VM
and yeah, things are good,

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:37.210
that's awesome.

00:10:37.210 --> 00:10:39.980
But if things don't
look good, you also

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:42.860
want to see, hey, what's the
serial console output, right?

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:47.180
And we have that right
there in our Cloud Console

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:48.980
you can click on
serial console access

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:50.854
and kind of see what's
going on with your VM.

00:10:50.854 --> 00:10:53.607
Did it boot correctly, did the
license get assigned correctly,

00:10:53.607 --> 00:10:55.440
is it authenticated,
and so on and so forth.

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:59.330
So lots of great tools
and ways in which

00:10:59.330 --> 00:11:02.120
you can spin up your Windows
VMs and see that things

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:03.560
are working well.

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:05.360
FRANCESC COMPOY: So
after what you said,

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:08.960
I have, like, 100 questions.

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:11.570
The first one being you
mentioned PowerShell, and that

00:11:11.570 --> 00:11:13.370
made me think about
the fact that now you

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:15.560
can run Bash on
Windows apparently,

00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:16.894
but only on some versions of it.

00:11:16.894 --> 00:11:17.893
MARK MANDEL: Windows 10.

00:11:17.893 --> 00:11:20.180
FRANCESC COMPOY: So what
are the versions supported

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:21.770
on Google Cloud Platform?

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:26.090
AMRUTA GULANIKAR: So we support
